00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:04.610 align:start position:0%
researchers have discovered that at  least one shark species tends towards  vegetarianism the meter-long bonnethead  shark which sticks close to shore and  hunts in shallow water usually feasts on  shrimp small crabs and fish found in  seagrass meadows however researchers  realize that juvenile bonnethead  stomachs could contain more sea grass  than critters so a graduate student fed  several sharks a diet of 90% eel grass  and 10% squid despite this mostly  vegetarian fare all the Sharks gained  weight they were digesting at least half  the seagrass they were eating that's on  par with juvenile sea turtles which are  well-known to rely on eating sea grass  this is a bit puzzling because the  bonnethead has the same shortcut as its  Hammerhead relatives and usually plant  eaters evolved longer guts so  researchers suspect that microbes in the  bonnethead shark are doing the digesting  for it no other sharks are known to eat  plants though whale sharks hunt  microscopic animals floating in the  water and may also consume some  microscopic plants but it's not clear if  they're digesting those plants because  seagrass meadows are so important for  filtering water removing carbon dioxide  from the air adding lots of oxygen  instead understanding the role of these  sharks in these Meadows is very  important  you  [Music]  [Music]
 

